sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant FE as Frontend (React)
    participant BE as Backend (Express)
    participant DB as Database (Aiven MySQL via Prisma)
    participant Mail as Email Service

    Note over User,Mail: Request a reset link
    User->>FE: Enter email, submit "Forgot Password"
    FE->>BE: POST /api/auth/forgot-password {email}
    Note over BE: passwordResetRateLimit middleware -- max 5 attempts / 15 min / IP
    BE->>DB: findUnique User by email
    alt no such user
        BE-->>FE: 200 generic "If that email exists, a reset link was sent"
        Note over BE,FE: Same response either way -- prevents confirming which emails are registered
    else user exists
        BE->>BE: Generate random reset token, hash it
        BE->>DB: Store hashed token + expiry on User
        BE->>Mail: Send reset link containing the raw token
        BE-->>FE: 200 generic "If that email exists, a reset link was sent"
    end

    Note over User,Mail: Complete the reset
    User->>FE: Open link from email, enter new password
    FE->>BE: POST /api/auth/reset-password {token, newPassword}
    BE->>DB: Look up user by hashed token
    alt token not found or expired
        BE-->>FE: 400 "Invalid or expired reset link"
    else token valid
        BE->>BE: bcrypt.hash(newPassword)
        BE->>DB: Update User.passwordHash, clear token, mustChangePassword = false
        BE->>DB: writeAuditLog(PASSWORD_RESET)
        BE-->>FE: 200 "Password updated, please log in"
    end

    Note over User,DB: Change password while logged in (self-service)
    User->>FE: Enter current password + new password
    FE->>BE: POST /api/auth/change-password {currentPassword, newPassword}
    BE->>DB: findUnique current user, bcrypt.compare(currentPassword)
    alt current password does not match
        BE-->>FE: 401 "Current password is incorrect"
    else matches
        BE->>DB: Update User.passwordHash, mustChangePassword = false
        BE-->>FE: 200 "Password changed"
    end
